WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.280
With eight narratively complex seasons under
its belt, American Horror Story has left us

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.110
with a number of doozies to puzzle over.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.720
With that in mind, here's a look at this long-running
hit anthology's biggest unanswered questions

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:11.920
and there's more than a few.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.120
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.620
Murder House, American Horror Story's first
season, set the foundation for the series

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:21.810
by introducing us to the Montgomery House,
an infamous mansion in Los Angeles with a

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.320
disturbingly high death count and a history
of violence that goes all the way back to

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.900
its first owners in 1922: Dr. Charles Montgomery
played by Matt Ross and his wife Nora played

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:31.940
by Lily Rabe.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:37.080
Dr. Montgomery, a surgeon to all of Hollywood's
finest in the 1920s, built the Victorian home

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:37.760
for his wife.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.180
He never fails to remind her, and it always
fails to impress her.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.040
"I built you this house, exactly the way you
wanted it."

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.520
"And how many servants do we have?

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:47.440
Two?"

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.380
When they fell on hard times, Nora decided
that Charles should start offering abortions

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.380
out of the basement.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.440
"No one will ever know…

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.580
But we do require payment up front."

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.420
After an abortion went very wrong, Charles
was exposed and the father of the baby dismembered

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.619
the Montgomery's newborn in retaliation.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:06.300
"Charles…?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Oh my god."

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.200
Crazed with grief, Charles sewed the baby
back together and reanimated it.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.620
The child was bloodthirsty, and Nora ended
up killing all three of them.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.340
Their ghosts continue to haunt the house…
along with anyone else who died there.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.840
Were these terrible events enough to shatter
a psychic veil and create the house where

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.200
the eventual Antichrist would be conceived
and born?

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.260
Or was there something more?

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:30.520
This vital question to the entire AHS arc
has never been answered.

00:01:31.539 --> 00:01:35.130
If people kept going missing after booking
a stay at a particular hotel, you'd think

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.620
the place would be positively crawling with
law enforcement…

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.720
But no, not at the Hotel Cortez.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.320
"I need a room, one night."

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.540
"$150."

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.759
"Says here $30."

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:44.340
"That's out of date."

00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:50.419
Like Murder House, the hotel racks up an enormous
body count due to the evil energy of the place,

00:01:50.419 --> 00:01:54.539
yet people keep booking stays at the Cortez…
and when they die terribly and violently within

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.860
its walls, nobody seems to come looking for
them there.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.860
Does this have something to do with an enchantment
on the site laid by the vampire Countess,

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:01.740
played by Lady Gaga?

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:05.779
She's been in the fashion industry for decades,
yet nobody seems bothered that she doesn't

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:06.280
age.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.899
Did she cast a glamour over herself as well
as the hotel?

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:13.489
Is this somehow related to Gaga's role as
the original Supreme Scathach in Roanoke ? Something

00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:14.820
definitely seems to be up.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.200
After all, the Robichaux witches even know
Queenie is there, and yet nobody goes looking

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:19.700
for her.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.600
That may be due to some sort of black magic.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.100
And consider this.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.940
When Will Drake is killed at the hotel, his
son Lachlan is also staying at the hotel but

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:28.460
we never see Lachlan again.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.460
Did the Countess turn him into one of the
ravaging vampire children?

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.440
Is he still there and is he still alive?

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:34.500
We just don't know.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.820
We will… probably never know, will we?

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:41.080
American Horror Story: Asylum is packed to
the brim with bizarre occurrences.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.980
We meet a supposed Anne Frank who lived.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.440
We get acquainted with the serial killer Bloody
Face.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:49.760
We witness the evildoing of a Nazi doctor,
who continues his vile medical experiments

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:50.520
on patients.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.459
But one of the plot threads that still leaves
us scratching our heads involves Kit Walker

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:57.220
played by Evan Peters and his abduction by
aliens.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.920
After his supposed abduction and return, his
wife also disappears.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:05.520
Authorities arrest Kit under suspicion of
being serial rapist and murderer Bloody Face.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:10.120
Kit is locked away in Briarcliff Asylum, and
nobody believes his alien abduction story.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.140
"Your story about little green men - no, that
won't do here."

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.140
"They weren't human."

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.920
He suffers terribly for crimes he didn't commit.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.629
We never get a definitive answer about the
aliens in American Horror Story, but Ryan

00:03:22.629 --> 00:03:26.280
Murphy discussed the puzzling plotline with
Entertainment Weekly, explaining that:

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.920
"For me, [aliens] were always an obvious metaphor
for God.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.400
It fit very easily into the world of a Catholic
sanitarium asylum.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.639
[...] It was also about science versus faith
so it made sense to me."

00:03:35.639 --> 00:03:38.719
Still, we'd like to know what these malignant
extraterrestrials were up to.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.320
Then again, aliens are notorious for their
wild ways.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:46.720
American Horror Story: Roanoke features Uber
driver Rhett Snow played by actor Billy Snow

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.390
and he seems to be the only working driver
in the area.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.960
He gives Cricket a ride, almost killing Flora
by accident in the process.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:54.780
"You know, I just prayed to god everyone was
alright."

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:58.950
He also gives Dylan a ride back to Mott Manor,
evidently totally fine with the fact that

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.340
the guy is wearing a Pig Man mask.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:05.329
Rhett shares the same last name as the fashionista
witch Myrtle Snow, and his first name is shared

00:04:05.329 --> 00:04:08.940
by Rhett Butler in Gone With the Wind, one
of Clark Gable's most famous roles.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.700
Could Rhett Snow be a member of Myrtle's extended
family?

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.540
Giving him an old-fashioned name would be
such a Myrtle thing to do.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.460
Are other members the Snow family similarly
driven by glamour and glitz… and were they

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.509
eager to name Rhett after a pop culture figure
from days of yore?

00:04:21.509 --> 00:04:24.500
If so, is Rhett possibly a warlock like his
witch relative?

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.160
Will he feature in a future season?

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.220
We probably wouldn't have seen him so many
times without a reason… but what is that

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:30.720
reason?

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.320
In a horrifying reveal during American Horror
Story: Murder House, we discover that the

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:39.620
latex-clad Rubber Man is, in fact, the ghost
of Tate Langdon, and he's the one who forced

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:42.360
himself upon Vivien, impregnating her with
Satan.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.660
So who is the second Rubber Man in Apocalypse?

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.240
It doesn't seem to be Michael, because he's
walking the halls and interviewing people

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:52.090
in Outpost 3 around the time Rubber Man is
doing his sexy business.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.980
Then again, Rubber Man clearly gets around.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:58.360
Gallant and the second Rubber Man have sex,
and later on, Gallant is startled when Michael

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.420
claims it wasn't him in the rubber suit.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.140
"You're pathetic."

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.560
When Gallant sees the Rubber Man again, he
stabs him in a fit of rage.

00:05:05.569 --> 00:05:07.420
But beneath the mask, it's not a man at all.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:11.260
No, it's Gallant's grandmother Bubbles, played
by the legendary Joan Collins!

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:13.180
It's a pretty eventful night, all told.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:16.900
Was the second Rubber Man even real, or was
he merely a hallucination?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.979
It's ironic that Evan Peters played the original
Rubber Man in Murder House, only to be on

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:23.060
the receiving end of his assault in Apocalypse.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.960
Time really is a flat circle, huh?

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:29.200
American Horror Story: Apocalypse spends a
great deal of time and attention on Emily

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.980
and Timothy, the star-crossed lovers in the
end times living in Outpost 3.

00:05:33.169 --> 00:05:36.360
When they're captured and taken underground,
they're both told that they were selected

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.440
for their excellent genes.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.120
"The elite.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:41.420
The worthy.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.400
Those chosen to survive."

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.120
Their forbidden love only draws them closer
together.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.550
By the end of Apocalypse and after the time
reset, we learn Emily has given birth to the

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:53.320
next Antichrist.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.580
Why were they included in the apocalypse bunker?

00:05:55.909 --> 00:05:59.860
Did someone know Emily and Timothy were destined
to sire an Antichrist in the event of a time

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:02.180
spell being cast to destroy young Michael
Langdon?

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:05.660
Was Outpost 3 hoping for another devil child
to rule the end of the world?

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:09.490
Or does this mean that the forces that are
trying to foster the Antichrist are well aware

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.680
of multiple timelines?

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.410
Also, Emily and Timothy are both human and
Satan must be conceived with human and spirit,

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:16.410
like Michael was.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.100
So, is one of them not who they say they are?

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.940
Could one of them have been under an identity
spell all along?

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:22.260
So many questions.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:26.940
American Horror Story: Hotel ended with a
number of pressing questions that were never

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:27.440
resolved.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:31.919
For example, what happened to the Countess'
disfigured vampire baby Bartholemew after

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.430
she was killed on the property and became
one of its ghosts?

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.240
What was the significance of the recurring
2:25 hour?

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.560
Oh, and we have some questions about that
gang of real-life serial killers.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:44.610
Each year on Halloween, they somehow manage
to visit James March, the man who built the

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:45.260
Hotel Cortez.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:50.580
As you no doubt recall, Richard Ramirez, Aileen
Wuornos, John Wayne Gacy, Jeffrey Dahmer,

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:54.960
and a masked Zodiac killer all attend a dinner
party in celebration of Devil's Night.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:56.540
"I don't get you, man.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:58.780
The real fun starts after you get caught.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:06:59.780
Don't you know that?"

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:02.340
Each year they drink absinthe and murder together
with glee.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.900
But none of these serial killers happened
to die in the Hotel Cortez, obviously.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:07.220
So how do they get there?

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.640
And where are they all chillaxing the rest
of the year?

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:13.010
In the world of American Horror Story, ghosts
tend to stay where they were killed… but

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.360
not these prolific murderers.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.420
What allows these serial killers to go and
join James March at the Cortez for one night

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:18.920
a year?

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.540
Does he have some witchy powers that are never
discussed?

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.480
Or is there something else behind their ability
to roam about freely?

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:25.740
Can other ghosts do this?

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:29.540
Fingers crossed for a future season that clears
up these unanswered questions from American

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:30.830
Horror Story's fifth season.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:31.820
Theories, anyone?

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:37.500
In American Horror Story: Coven, Evan Peters
plays Kyle Spencer, the president of a college

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:38.060
fraternity.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:42.660
When Madison and Zoe go to a raging party,
Madison is drugged and sexually assaulted

00:07:42.669 --> 00:07:45.659
by a bunch of frat guys until Kyle intervenes.

00:07:45.659 --> 00:07:49.979
Madison is so furious about the attack, she
uses her powers to flip over the frat boys'

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:53.360
bus, killing a great many of them and also
killing poor sweet Kyle.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:57.629
Feeling guilty about Kyle's death, Madison
and Zoe visit the morgue and decide to resurrect

00:07:57.629 --> 00:08:00.840
him … but there's a problem: The boys were
all left in pieces.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:04.940
Madison finds Kyle's head and then picks choice
body parts from the various dead frat boys…

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:07.940
in order to create what we'll respectfully
call "Franken-Kyle."

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:12.490
The spell doesn't seem to work at first, but
when it does, Kyle clearly isn't the same

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:13.820
kind-hearted guy he was before.

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:17.900
He eventually regains his strength and ability
to speak, and by the end of the season, he

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:22.040
becomes becomes the Miss Robichaux Academy's
butler and protector as Spalding had been.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:26.180
We return to Robichaux in American Horror
Story: Apocalypse, but there's no sign of

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.060
Kyle at all.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:31.540
Evan Peters is all over Apocalypse in fact,
he plays four different roles throughout the

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:36.060
season: Mr. Gallant, James Patrick March,
Tate Langdon, and Jeff Pfister.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:39.890
So it's really rather odd that Franken-Kyle
doesn't make a single appearance throughout

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:40.420
the season.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:41.680
What happened to him?

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:42.600
Did he die again?

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.200
Or could Ryan Murphy be saving him for a future
season?

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:46.240
Time will tell.

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:50.310
What was the witch Mallory's real identity
and why was she so powerful?

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:53.630
We know that Queenie's lineage goes all the
way back to the Salem witch trials.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.960
Misty Dawn comes from a long line of swamp
witches.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:09:01.000
Supreme Fiona and her daughter Cordelia are
both white witch royalty, as are Madison Montgomery

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:01.580
and Zoe.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:05.580
But we know virtually nothing about Mallory,
or her past when we meet her as a personal

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:08.390
assistant in American Horror Story: Apocalypse.

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:11.280
"Are the Kardashians filming out there?"

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:15.250
She was functioning under an identity-cloaking
spell, so it makes sense that she didn't know

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:18.220
who or what she was, yet it seems nobody else
knew either.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:23.460
Apocalypse never really addresses her identity
or lineage at all, which is surprising: People

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:26.500
with her level of immense power tend to rise
from well-known bloodlines.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.420
This begs the question: Is Mallory even a
witch at all?

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:31.760
We need Ryan Murphy to circle back around
to this one.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:36.850
We learn in American Horror Story: Coven that
there can be only one Supreme at a time, and

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:40.560
when her powers and health begin to weaken
it means another Supreme is on the rise.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:45.140
Fiona had to die in order for her daughter
Cordelia to ascend, just as Cordelia has to

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.680
die for Mallory to take her powers.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:51.200
But in American Horror Story: Roanoke, many
of the terrible events are set in motion by

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.230
the wood witch Scathach, who they say is the
original Supreme.

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:56.340
But how can that be if there's only one at
a time?

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:57.940
Is she a ghost Supreme?

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:00.300
Does being the first give her exceptional
powers?

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.700
We demand answers!

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:04.500
